{
  "name": "CoolFix - WhatsApp AI Customer Service",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "httpMethod": "POST",
        "path": "whatsapp",
        "responseMode": "responseNode",
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "node-webhook",
      "name": "WhatsApp Inbound (Webhook)",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.webhook",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [-40, 300],
      "webhookId": "coolfix-whatsapp"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "// Parse the Meta WhatsApp Cloud API payload into a simple shape.\nconst out = [];\nfor (const item of $input.all()) {\n  const body = item.json.body || item.json;\n  const entries = body.entry || [];\n  for (const entry of entries) {\n    for (const change of (entry.changes || [])) {\n      const value = change.value || {};\n      const contacts = {};\n      for (const c of (value.contacts || [])) contacts[c.wa_id] = (c.profile||{}).name;\n      for (const msg of (value.messages || [])) {\n        if (msg.type !== 'text') continue;\n        out.push({ json: {\n          wa_number: msg.from,\n          text: msg.text.body,\n          name: contacts[msg.from] || null,\n          wa_message_id: msg.id\n        }});\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}\nreturn out.length ? out : [{ json: { skip: true } }];"
      },
      "id": "node-parse",
      "name": "Parse WhatsApp Message",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [200, 300]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "url": "={{ $env.APP_BASE_URL || 'http://host.docker.internal:8000' }}/api/business",
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "node-knowledge",
      "name": "Retrieve Business Knowledge",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
      "typeVersion": 4.2,
      "position": [440, 300]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "method": "POST",
        "url": "https://api.openai.com/v1/chat/completions",
        "sendHeaders": true,
        "headerParameters": {
          "parameters": [
            { "name": "Authorization", "value": "=Bearer {{ $env.OPENAI_API_KEY }}" },
            { "name": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }
          ]
        },
        "sendBody": true,
        "specifyBody": "json",
        "jsonBody": "={\n  \"model\": \"gpt-4o-mini\",\n  \"response_format\": { \"type\": \"json_object\" },\n  \"temperature\": 0.3,\n  \"messages\": [\n    { \"role\": \"system\", \"content\": \"You are the intent classifier for CoolFix Services. Return ONLY JSON: {\\\"intent\\\": one of [greeting,faq,pricing,service_info,booking,complaint,new_lead,recommendation,human_support,emergency,unknown], \\\"confidence\\\": 0-1, \\\"requires_human\\\": boolean, \\\"service\\\": slug or null}. Ground yourself in this business knowledge: \" + JSON.stringify($node[\"Retrieve Business Knowledge\"].json) },\n    { \"role\": \"user\", \"content\": {{ JSON.stringify($json.text) }} }\n  ]\n}",
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "node-ai-intent",
      "name": "AI Intent Detection (OpenAI)",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
      "typeVersion": 4.2,
      "position": [680, 300]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "// Merge the classifier result back with the message fields.\nconst msg = $node[\"Parse WhatsApp Message\"].json;\nlet parsed = {};\ntry { parsed = JSON.parse($json.choices[0].message.content); } catch (e) { parsed = { intent: 'unknown', confidence: 0 }; }\nreturn [{ json: { ...msg, ...parsed } }];"
      },
      "id": "node-merge",
      "name": "Structure Intent",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [900, 300]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "rules": {
          "values": [
            { "conditions": { "options": { "caseSensitive": false }, "conditions": [ { "leftValue": "={{ $json.intent }}", "rightValue": "emergency", "operator": { "type": "string", "operation": "equals" } } ] }, "outputKey": "Emergency" },
            { "conditions": { "options": { "caseSensitive": false }, "conditions": [ { "leftValue": "={{ $json.requires_human }}", "rightValue": true, "operator": { "type": "boolean", "operation": "true" } } ] }, "outputKey": "Human Handoff" },
            { "conditions": { "options": { "caseSensitive": false }, "conditions": [ { "leftValue": "={{ $json.intent }}", "rightValue": "booking", "operator": { "type": "string", "operation": "equals" } } ] }, "outputKey": "Booking" }
          ]
        },
        "options": { "fallbackOutput": "extra" }
      },
      "id": "node-switch",
      "name": "Route by Intent",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.switch",
      "typeVersion": 3,
      "position": [1120, 300]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {},
      "id": "node-emergency",
      "name": "Emergency: alert + handoff",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.noOp",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [1360, 100]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {},
      "id": "node-human",
      "name": "Human Handoff: notify operator",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.noOp",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [1360, 260]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {},
      "id": "node-booking",
      "name": "Booking: collect slots + book",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.noOp",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [1360, 420]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {},
      "id": "node-info",
      "name": "FAQ / Pricing / Info",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.noOp",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [1360, 580]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "method": "POST",
        "url": "={{ $env.APP_BASE_URL || 'http://host.docker.internal:8000' }}/api/simulator/message",
        "sendBody": true,
        "specifyBody": "json",
        "jsonBody": "={\n  \"wa_number\": {{ JSON.stringify($json.wa_number) }},\n  \"text\": {{ JSON.stringify($json.text) }},\n  \"name\": {{ JSON.stringify($json.name) }}\n}",
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "node-process",
      "name": "Generate Reply, Send & Store (App)",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
      "typeVersion": 4.2,
      "position": [1600, 300]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "respondWith": "json",
        "responseBody": "={{ { \"status\": \"ok\", \"intent\": $json.result.intent, \"reply\": $json.result.reply } }}",
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "node-respond",
      "name": "Respond to WhatsApp",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.respondToWebhook",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [1840, 300]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## CoolFix WhatsApp AI - Orchestration\nThis workflow mirrors the in-app orchestrator:\n1. **Webhook** receives the Meta WhatsApp event\n2. **Parse** normalises the payload\n3. **Retrieve Business Knowledge** pulls CoolFix's real info (no hallucination)\n4. **AI Intent Detection** returns structured JSON\n5. **Route by Intent** branches: emergency / human / booking / info\n6. **Generate Reply, Send & Store** calls the app, which produces the grounded reply, sends via WhatsApp and persists everything\n7. **Respond** closes the webhook\n\nSet env vars in n8n: `OPENAI_API_KEY`, `APP_BASE_URL`.\nError handling: attach an *Error Trigger* workflow or enable *Retry On Fail* on the HTTP nodes.",
        "height": 340,
        "width": 420
      },
      "id": "node-note",
      "name": "Docs",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [-40, -120]
    }
  ],
